{"id":108008,"docketId":1459868,"caseName":"Carlos v. New York","caseNameFull":"Carlos v. New York","slug":"carlos-v-new-york","docketNumber":"524","dateFiled":"1969-12-08","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1969,"scdbId":"1969-012","direction":"Liberal","votesMajority":6,"votesMinority":2,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":"Herald Price Fahringer and Eugene Gressman for petitioner.","natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":21,"judges":"However, Roth, Massachusetts","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":108008,"type":"majority","typeCode":"010combined","perCuriam":true,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1384,"isHtml":true,"text":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>\n<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"b227-9\">\n  Per Curiam.\n </author>\n<p id=\"b227-10\">\n  The petition for a writ of certiorari is granted and the judgment is reversed,\n  <em>\n   Redrup\n  </em>\n  v.\n  <em>\n   New York,\n  </em>\n  <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9423403\"><a href=\"/opinion/107426/redrup-v-new-york/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Redrup v. New York\">386 U. S. 767</a></span>.\n </p>\n<judges id=\"b227-11\">\n  The Chief Justice and Mr. Justice Harlan are of the opinion that certiorari should be denied. However, the case having been taken for review, they would affirm the judgment of the state court upon the premises stated in Mr. Justice Harlan\u2019s separate opinion in\n  <em>\n   Roth\n  </em>\n  v.\n  <em>\n   United States,\n  </em>\n  <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9421496\"><a href=\"/opinion/105547/roth-v-united-states/#496\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Roth v. United States\">354 U. S. 476, 496</a></span> (1957), and in his dissenting opinion in\n  <em>\n   Memoirs\n  </em>\n  v.\n  <em>\n   Massachusetts,\n  </em>\n  <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9423171\"><a href=\"/opinion/107187/a-book-named-john-clelands-memoirs-of-a-woman-of-pleasure-v-attorney/#455\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: A Book Named &quot;John Cleland&#x27;s Memoirs of a Woman of...\">383 U. S. 413, 455</a></span> (1966).\n </judges>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}